From: Uke contributors
Subject: [PATCH] iio: uke-ssc: wait for fresh streaming reports on buffer join

Only on-change streams can replay their admitted unchanged state. A streaming
sample may be old when another owner joins; do not stamp that cache with the
new subscription time. Preserve demand, raw ABI, rates and early-report ACK
ordering. Gravity and quaternion buffers receive the next actual report.

--- a/drivers/iio/common/uke-ssc/uke-ssc-iio.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/uke-ssc/uke-ssc-iio.c
@@ -1114,10 +1114,13 @@
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&c->state, flags);
 	} else {
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&c->state, flags);
-		/* Supply the current valid sample once when joining an unchanged
-		 * stream. An enable ACK that already published must not duplicate it.
+		/* Only an on-change subscription can replay its current state.
+		 * Streaming consumers wait for a new report instead of receiving an
+		 * old cached value stamped with the new subscription time. An enable
+		 * ACK that already published must not duplicate its first report.
 		 */
-		if (ssc_current(c) && s->ready && s->stream_active && !s->error &&
+		if (s->attributes.stream_type == 1 && ssc_current(c) &&
+		    s->ready && s->stream_active && !s->error &&
 		    s->ticks && s->registered && s->sample_sequence == sequence) {
 			s64 scan[SSC_SCAN_MAX] = {};
 
